::U6F1_01::Substance use is {=a broad term that does not automatically mean misuse ~always addiction ~always illegal ~always overdose}

::U6F1_02::Substance misuse includes {=taking another person's prescription ~following one's directions ~seeking help ~safe storage}

::U6F1_03::Tolerance means {=reduced response after repeated exposure ~increased safety ~recovery ~refusal}

::U6F1_04::Dependence may involve {=adaptation and withdrawal ~only peer pressure ~a legal status ~a marketing claim}

::U6F1_05::A risk factor {=increases vulnerability without guaranteeing an outcome ~proves a diagnosis ~cannot change ~is always genetic}

::U6F1_06::A protective factor is {=a supportive trusted adult ~peer pressure ~poor coping ~misinformation}

::U6F1_07::Which is valid reasoning? {=One warning sign does not diagnose a disorder; use qualified assessment ~One sign proves addiction ~Risk guarantees outcome ~Stigma improves care}
